<title>FRANCE: New York top originating gateway for imports Jan 9.</title>
<headline>New York top originating gateway for imports Jan 9.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top airport gateway for imports to Charles de Gaulle and Orly airports in January 1997.</p>
<p>The top ten airport gateways for ADP imports in tonnes for January 1997 with the percentage change on January 1996 were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  New York	    2,625     down  8.9pct</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	     2,186     up    3.1</p>
<p> 3  Tokyo		 1,573     up   59.5</p>
<p> 4  Hong Kong	   1,516     up    3.7</p>
<p> 5  Montreal	    1,335     down  5.7</p>
<p> 6  Los Angeles	  992	down 24.0</p>
<p> 7  Singapore	    672	up   84.5</p>
<p> 8  Seoul		  620	up   86.0</p>
<p> 9  Casblanca	    545	down 38.2</p>
<p> 10 Miami		  499	down 13.6</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
